.TH SUPIVPN-PROFILE 8 "October 2026" "SupiVPN" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
supivpn-profile \- initialize a VPN wrapping key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supivpn-profile
.B \-init
.BI \-server-key " file"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explicitly initializes a tls-crypt-v2 server wrapping key, preserving an
existing key. Client profiles require SAML-authorized download or Connect import
through the controller. Offline unbound issuance was removed in v0.10.0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-init
Initialize or validate the server wrapping key.
.TP
.BI \-server-key " file"
Wrapping key path. Default: /var/lib/supivpn/tls-crypt-v2-server.key.
For the combined Debian installation, explicitly select
/etc/supivpn/keys/tls-crypt-v2-server.key and follow the documented ownership rules.
.TP
.BI \-openvpn " file"
Absolute OpenVPN executable path. Default: /usr/sbin/openvpn.
.TP
.BI \-secret-arn " arn"
Use an AWS Secrets Manager cluster wrapping key. Only valid with \-init.
This is an explicit external credential operation, not part of package setup.
.TP
.B \-h
Show command-line help.
.SH NOTES
The initial implementation requires the tested OpenVPN Community 2.7.8.
Package installation never invokes this command or creates keys.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR supivpn (8),
